Tekrion is dual-use developer observability software.

This package provides a local HTTP proxy that can record explicitly configured
OpenAI-compatible and Anthropic Messages API traffic. It also provides an
authenticated local service for storing, querying, reporting on, archiving, and
retaining that evidence.

The intended use is consensual debugging, auditing, and incident review of AI
coding agents in workspaces and accounts the operator is authorized to inspect.
It is not intended for covert monitoring, credential theft, unauthorized traffic
interception, exploitation, or bypassing access controls.

The control service and recorder proxy bind to loopback by default. Non-loopback
proxy use requires an explicit opt-in. Recorded traffic can contain source code,
prompts, model responses, tool activity, credentials, and other sensitive data.
Operators are responsible for obtaining authorization and applying Tekrion's
redaction, access-control, archive, and retention safeguards.
